Almanac: {
	Notes: {
		Foreword: {
			Title: A Word Before You Begin.
			Body:
				'''
				If you're reading this, then the assailants have done their work and I've done my dying. But you, my boy, have inherited the better half of me: this book.[p]I don't want you to worry! Everything I know about alchemy is in these pages, and everything I didn't... well, I've left room for you to fill in.
				The world out there is much bigger and stranger than the one I had at your age, and twice as full of things that yearn to be discovered.
				[p]The book sorts itself for you, so you needn't. Flip to Recipes to see everything you can brew; the little tabs down the side narrow it by discipline. Ingredients lists every reagent worth the name, tap one to learn its uses, though it will only speak of brews you've actually discovered. Secrets are earned, not handed over.
				[p]Drop a thing into the slot on the side and the book shows only what uses it. Most pages stay blank until you've earned them. So go and earn them.
				[p]Please, read this almanac when you're stuck, ignore me when you're not. And for the love of all that ferments, label your bottles.
				[p]I'll be rooting for 'ya, kid. I can already tell you're going to be a fantastic alchemist. - Uncle J.
				[p]Oh, and one more thing: if you find a woman named Argie, tell her I said hi. She was a good friend of mine, and I think she'd like to know that you found this book.
				'''
		}

		Principles: {
			Title: The Seven Principles.
			Body: Every substance leans toward one of seven natures. Learn to read them and you'll know the quality of a brew before you ever pour it. Here is the short of it, and how each tends to behave when it meets another:
		}

		Temperaments: {
			Title: The Six Temperaments.
			Body: Six temperaments, paired into three old quarrels. Every solute carries at least one, and every brew is the argument they have inside the bottle. Opposites sit across the wheel; the lines drawn between them are the meetings worth knowing.
		}

		Chemistry: {
			Title: Solvents & Solutes.
			Body: Three words you'll see on every page, so learn them once and be done with it. Get the pair right and the solution follows on its own.
		}

		OnPotency: {
			Title: On Potency...
			Body:
				'''
				Potency is not luck, it's measure. Every solute has a portion, and a station slot counts how many whole portions you've stacked into it. One portion, one star, up to five.
				[p]A recipe asks for a minimum and refuses you below it. Stack past that minimum and the extra stars are spent rather than wasted: they carry into the bottle as strength, and often as duration. You pay for them in leaves and stones, mind, so a five-star brew costs five times a one-star one.
				[p]The clever alchemist is not the one who always reaches for five stars, it's the one who knows when it is one.
				[p]As for those mundane solutions, don't snore at them! A blank page is where every story starts.
				[p]Speaking of, you need to create yourself an alchemy station to get started. I've already left you a cooking pot, I trust you can figure out the rest.
				'''
		}

		Lexicon: {
			Title: A Little Latin.
			Body: Half this trade is old words worn smooth by use. Here are the ones you'll meet on labels, in recipes, and carved into things that would rather you couldn't read them.
		}
	}
}
